# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first entry is the important one: a pnpm workspace's node_modules is a
# forest of absolute symlinks into .pnpm. Copying it from the host would either
# break (Linux container, Windows/macOS links) or — worse — silently work with
# whatever the host had installed, which is how "works on my machine" gets
# baked into an image. The image installs its own from the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — the image builds its own.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets never enter an image layer. Compose injects them as environment.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Host-side state
.git
.githooks
.docker-data
**/.data
*.log

# Not needed to build or run anything
.github
docs
*.pdf
**/README.md
